        <div class="tab-content active" id="tab-assessment" data-main="vulns" data-sub="assessment">
            <div class="info">
                Tick the locations to assess in the row above the table - the selection is remembered per browser.
                A rating you save applies to <strong>every selected location</strong> in which the finding occurs and
                needs a comment; a <strong>false positive</strong> needs no comment, is excluded from all counts and
                can be undone. The table sorts by <strong>effective severity</strong>, so your own ratings decide the
                order (inside one severity the higher CVSS comes first).
                <br><br>
                Opening this page and <em>Apply</em> read the <strong>stored</strong> result - instant, no device is
                touched. <em>Scan &amp; Review</em> is the only button that queries the devices; while it runs the
                server stays usable and a second panel joins the running pass. Scheduled scans keep the stored result
                fresh on their own.
            </div>

            <div class="locbar" id="locationPanel">
                <div class="locbar-head">
                    <span class="locbar-title">Locations to assess</span>
                    <span class="hint">selected: <b id="locCountTxt">all</b></span>
                    <label class="loc-all" data-help="loc.all"><input type="checkbox" id="locAll" checked> All locations</label>
                    <button id="locApply" class="green small" data-help="loc.apply">Apply</button>
                </div>
                <div id="locList" class="locbar-list">
                    {{#each meshList}}
                    <label class="loc-item"><input type="checkbox" class="loc-cb" value="{{this.id}}" checked> {{this.name}}</label>
                    {{/each}}
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="controls">
                <button id="scanBtn" data-help="scan.review">Scan &amp; Review</button>
                <span id="scanStatus"></span>
            </div>

            <div class="filter-row">
                <input type="text" id="filterText" class="filter-input" data-help="filter.text" placeholder="Filter by CVE, software, device, location...">
                <select id="filterSeverity" class="filter-select" data-help="filter.severity">
                    <option value="">All Severities</option>
                    <option value="CRITICAL">Critical</option>
                    <option value="HIGH">High</option>
                    <option value="MEDIUM">Medium</option>
                    <option value="LOW">Low</option>
                    <option value="UNKNOWN">Unknown</option>
                    <option value="false positive">False Positive</option>
                </select>
                <select id="filterStatus" class="filter-select" data-help="filter.status">
                    <option value="">All Statuses</option>
                    <option value="CVE">CVE</option>
                    <option value="false positive">False Positive</option>
                    <option value="rated">Rated</option>
                    <option value="unrated">Unrated</option>
                </select>
            </div>

            <div id="msg"></div>
            <div class="table-container" id="results"></div>
        </div>
